{#
    The mark in the line that sends a reader to the foot of the page.

    The core prints `node.value`, which is what the author typed between the
    brackets. For `[#note]_` that is `#note`, and the block at the foot of the
    page calls the same footnote `[1]`. A reader who looks for the note they
    just saw has nothing to match.

    The number is the target's and not the node's. A footnote written `[1]_`
    carries its own. One written `[#name]_` or `[#]_` gets its number while
    the document compiles, which is the whole reason to write it that way.
    Until then the node says nought. The target is what the compiler hands
    back once it has counted. So the question goes there first, and the
    node's own number is the fallback for the form that stated one.

    No class on the mark. It is a `<sup>` with a link in it, and the document
    layer already says what both of those are. A name here is a hook in the
    markup with nothing behind it, which is the one thing this theme must not
    write.
#}
{%- if node.internalTarget -%}
    <sup>[<a href="{{- renderTarget(node.internalTarget) -}}">{{- node.internalTarget.number|default(node.number) -}}</a>]</sup>
{%- else -%}
    <sup>[{{- node.number -}}]</sup>
{%- endif -%}
